      "description": "Watch Columbus Crew vs New England Revolution highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. The MLS spotlight fell on this compelling encounter on August 30, 2026 , as two ambitious sides clashed in a match defined by tactical shifts and clinical finishing. From the opening whistle, the energy in the stadium suggested a contest that would be decided by the smallest of margins. Early Breakthrough for Columbus Crew The home side, Columbus Crew , wasted no time in asserting their dominance, finding the back of the net just 8 minutes into the match. Mohamed Farsi provided a sharp assist to Brais Mendez , who clinical finish sent the home crowd into a frenzy. The early lead forced the visitors to rethink their approach, and the game grew increasingly physical, leading to a yellow card for Tarun Karumanchi in the 25th minute as the battle for midfield supremacy intensified. New England’s Resilient Response Refusing to be overwhelmed, New England Revolution began to find their rhythm and turned the tide before the halftime break. The equalizer arrived in the 32nd minute when Matt Polster converted a chance created by Mamadou Fofana . The momentum stayed with the visitors, and in the 41st minute, they took the lead. Carles Gil showcased his vision with a precise assist for Dor Turgeman , completing a swift turnaround that left the hosts searching for answers as they headed into the interval. Sealing the Victory The second half saw Columbus Crew attempt to claw their way back into the game, but their efforts were hampered by a disciplined opposition defense. After Alhassan Yusuf received a yellow card in the 78th minute, the New England Revolution put the result beyond doubt. In the 79th minute, Peyton Miller teed up Carles Gil , who added a goal to his earlier assist to make it 3-1. A flurry of late substitutions, including the introduction of Jackson Yueill and Diego Fagundez , ensured the visitors maintained their composure until the final whistle, securing a significant away win."
